From 9e35b8b46f5f74dfe3c1c5a2d6ba4e5cf70bd128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:35:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Plugin: do not report MLD link AccessPoint.Status as
 Disabled on txPower==0

wifiGen_vap_status() (src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c) requires GET_INTERFACE
tx power != 0 before it will report an AccessPoint as Enabled. For an
AP MLD link, wld_ssid_nl80211_getInterfaceInfoExt()
(src/nl80211/wld_ssid_nl80211.c:74-125) overrides ifaceInfo.txPower
with the per-link value found in the NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS nest
(:112-118), taken from link[NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY_TX_POWER_LEVEL]
(src/nl80211/wld_nl80211_parser.c:328).

Upstream nl80211/backports-6.12.96 never sets that attribute inside a
link nest; nl80211_send_iface() only puts MLO_LINK_ID, MAC and chandef
per link and reports WIPHY_TX_POWER_LEVEL solely at the top level
(net/wireless/nl80211.c:4071-4100 vs. :4025-4031). So for every MLD
link (including the primary, linkId 0) ifaceInfo.txPower is always 0,
the "power down" ASSERTS at wifiGen_vap.c:128 fires silently, and
AP.1/AP.3/AP.5 (and any other MLD-affiliated AccessPoint) never leave
Disabled, even though hostapd already reports AP-ENABLED for that
link. QCA's vendor backport used on Freedom boards does report
per-link tx power there, so real boards are unaffected; this hits any
upstream-mac80211 MLO platform running pWHM.

Skip the check for MLD links instead: ifaceInfo.nMloLinks > 0 is the
same "this is an MLD link" indicator s_getVapEnable() already uses
below. This is a workaround (A) pending a kernel-side fix that backports
upstream's per-link GET_INTERFACE tx power into
package/kernel/mac80211's backports-6.12.96 (workaround B); B was
prototyped and found to regress live AP status checks (pWHM's nl80211
parser trips on the added per-link nest attribute), so this workaround
stays in place until B is reworked.
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c
index fd153b9e37c7..d51747d1a895 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c
@@ -125,7 +125,18 @@ int wifiGen_vap_status(T_AccessPoint* pAP) {
     ASSERTS_FALSE(rc < SWL_RC_OK, false, ME, "%s: Fail to get nl80211 ap iface info", pAP->alias);
     ASSERTS_STR(ifaceInfo.ssid, false, ME, "%s: ssid down", pAP->alias);
     ASSERTS_NOT_EQUALS(ifaceInfo.chanSpec.ctrlFreq, 0, false, ME, "%s: radio down", pAP->alias);
-    ASSERTS_NOT_EQUALS(ifaceInfo.txPower, 0, false, ME, "%s: power down", pAP->alias);
+    /*
+     * Upstream nl80211/backports-6.12 (our kernel backport - QCA's vendor
+     * backport used on Freedom boards is not affected) never reports
+     * WIPHY_TX_POWER_LEVEL inside the per-link NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS nest
+     * returned by NL80211_CMD_GET_INTERFACE; it is only ever set at the top
+     * level. For MLD link VAPs, wld_ssid_nl80211_getInterfaceInfoExt()
+     * (src/nl80211/wld_ssid_nl80211.c) overwrites ifaceInfo.txPower with
+     * that always-0 per-link value, so this check must be skipped for MLD
+     * links. ifaceInfo.nMloLinks > 0 is the same "this is an MLD link"
+     * indicator already used by s_getVapEnable() below.
+     */
+    ASSERTS_TRUE((ifaceInfo.txPower != 0) || (ifaceInfo.nMloLinks > 0), false, ME, "%s: power down", pAP->alias);
     int ret = wld_linuxIfUtils_getLinkState(wld_rad_getSocket(pAP->pRadio), ifaceInfo.name);
     ASSERTI_FALSE(ret <= 0, false, ME, "%s: link down", pAP->alias);
     ASSERT_TRUE(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_isReady(pAP->wpaCtrlInterface), false, ME, "%s: wpaCtrl not ready", pAP->alias);
